---
layout: layouts/feature.njk
wide: true
title: Storage | Shellui
description: Attach a private company bucket with storage-service. Apps upload and share files through the SDK, with access grants, share links, and quotas.
eyebrow: Features
heading: Company storage in the shell
lede: Connect storage-service and the shell owns the company bucket. Iframe apps upload, list, and pick files through the SDK. New files stay private until you share them.
---

<div class="grid items-start gap-10 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:gap-16">
  <div class="max-w-2xl">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-foreground sm:text-3xl">A company bucket behind the host</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">The <a class="font-medium text-primary-ink underline underline-offset-2 dark:text-primary" href="{{ site.storageService }}">storage-service</a> is a Django API with a Supabase-compatible surface at <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">/storage/v1/*</code>. It verifies identity-service JWTs, stores blobs in S3 or on disk, and enforces company and optional per-user quotas.</p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">Embedded apps do not call that API themselves. They use <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">shellui.storage</code>. The SDK posts to the root shell, which runs the request with <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">storage.url</code> and the signed-in user's token.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-xs">
    {% include "feature-visual-storage.njk" %}
  </div>
</div>

<div class="mt-10 grid max-w-3xl gap-6 sm:grid-cols-3">
  <div>
    <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-primary-ink dark:text-primary">1. Set storage.url</p>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm/6 text-muted-foreground">Add the storage-service origin. Optionally set <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 text-[0.8rem]">filesUrl</code> for the Files explorer and picker.</p>
  </div>
  <div>
    <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-primary-ink dark:text-primary">2. Read quota in Settings</p>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm/6 text-muted-foreground">Signed-in users open Settings, then Storage. Hide that page with <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 text-[0.8rem]">showInSettings: false</code> if you only want Admin and the SDK.</p>
  </div>
  <div>
    <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-primary-ink dark:text-primary">3. Call the SDK</p>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm/6 text-muted-foreground">After <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 text-[0.8rem]">init</code>, upload, list, move, and download through <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 text-[0.8rem]">shellui.storage.from("company")</code>.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="mt-8 max-w-3xl">
  {% highlight "ts", "shellui.config.ts" %}
import type { ShellUIConfig } from "@shellui/core";

const config: ShellUIConfig = {
  storage: {
    url: "http://localhost:8001",
    filesUrl: "http://localhost:5175/",
  },
};

export default config;
  {% endhighlight %}
</div>

<section class="mt-16" aria-labelledby="files-screenshot-slot">
  <h2 id="files-screenshot-slot" class="sr-only">Files screenshot slot</h2>
  {% set slotKind = "screenshot" %}
  {% set slotLabel = "Playground Files explorer" %}
  {% set slotHint = "16:9 · company bucket in host chrome. Not a generated mock." %}
  {% set slotRatio = "video" %}
  {% include "media-slot.njk" %}
</section>

<section class="mt-20" aria-labelledby="files-from-iframe">
  <div class="max-w-2xl">
    <h2 id="files-from-iframe" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-foreground sm:text-3xl">Files from the iframe</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">Methods return <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">{ data, error }</code> and do not throw. Nested folders are path segments. The picker opens the Files app in a shell modal so you can choose files or folders without building a browser.</p>
  </div>
  {% include "storage-sdk-examples.njk" %}
</section>

<section class="mt-20" aria-labelledby="private-by-default">
  <div class="max-w-2xl">
    <h2 id="private-by-default" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-foreground sm:text-3xl">Private by default</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">There is one system bucket per company, named <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">company</code>. New folders and files belong to the creator until you add an access grant. Nested items inherit the parent folder. There is no anonymous public bucket - use a share link for people outside the company.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-1 gap-10 md:grid-cols-3 md:gap-6 lg:gap-8">
    <div>
      <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-foreground">Access grants</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm/6 text-muted-foreground">Allow or deny <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 text-[0.8rem]">read</code>, <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 text-[0.8rem]">write</code>, or <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 text-[0.8rem]">admin</code> for a user, group, or the whole company, on a folder or a file.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-foreground">Share links</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm/6 text-muted-foreground">Secret URLs for one file, with an expiry and/or a download cap. No account required. Revoke them when the review is over.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-foreground">Quotas</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm/6 text-muted-foreground">A company total, plus an optional per-user cap. Overflow returns <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 text-[0.8rem]">413</code>. Settings shows usage to the signed-in user.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  {% include "storage-access-examples.njk" %}
</section>

